# Sanhedrin LLM - Deep Learning Hebrew Fragment Classification

## Vollständig trainiertes Modell auf realen Daten

**Schritt-für-Schritt-Anleitung für github.com/Rosary-mom/RosaryxAI und codespaces-jupyter**

### Voraussetzungen
- Python 3.10+
- PyTorch, torchvision, Pillow, scikit-learn
- GPU empfohlen (CUDA)
- Datensatz: Cambridge Genizah oder Genizat Germania Fragmente (Download: https://cudl.lib.cam.ac.uk/ oder Kaggle 'Hebrew Paleography')

### Schritt 1: Datensatz vorbereiten (reale Daten)
```python
import os
from torchvision import datasets, transforms

# Beispiel: Lade Patches aus lokalem Ordner 'geniza_patches/'
# Struktur: geniza_patches/Ashkenazic_Square/img1.jpg, ...
data_dir = 'geniza_patches'
transform = transforms.Compose([
    transforms.Resize((224, 224)),
    transforms.ToTensor(),
    transforms.Normalize([0.485, 0.456, 0.406], [0.229, 0.224, 0.225])
])
dataset = datasets.ImageFolder(data_dir, transform=transform)
train_loader = torch.utils.data.DataLoader(dataset, batch_size=32, shuffle=True)
```

### Schritt 2: Transfer-Learning von vortrainiertem Modell
```python
import torch
import torch.nn as nn
from torchvision import models

model = models.resnet18(pretrained=True)
model.fc = nn.Linear(model.fc.in_features, 14)  # 14 Klassen
model = model.to(device)

# Fine-Tuning nur der letzten Layer
for param in model.parameters():
    param.requires_grad = False
for param in model.fc.parameters():
    param.requires_grad = True

optimizer = torch.optim.Adam(model.fc.parameters(), lr=0.001)
```

